#: R/interrater.b.R
msgid ""
"Category “{cat}” accounts for {pct}% of every rating issued across all {k} "
"raters — a markedly uneven distribution. This is exactly the condition under "
"which Kappa becomes conservative: when nearly every case falls in one "
"category, the “chance agreement” Kappa subtracts is already high, leaving "
"little room for Kappa to register genuine agreement even when raters are "
"truly consistent (Gwet, 2014). AC1/AC2 and Krippendorff's α are not "
"penalized this way."
