#: R/internalconsistency.b.R
msgid ""
"Cronbach's α ({alpha}) and McDonald's ω ({omega}) differ by more than .04. α "
"assumes equal item loadings (τ-equivalence); "
msgstr ""

#: R/internalconsistency.b.R
msgid ""
"Cronbach's α and McDonald's ω agree closely — the τ-equivalence assumption "
"behind α looks reasonable here."
msgstr ""

#: R/internalconsistency.b.R
msgid ""
"Cronbach's α is the most commonly reported reliability coefficient and also "
"the most assumption-laden: it equals the true reliability only when items "
"are tau-equivalent (equal true-score loadings on a single common factor) "
"(Cronbach, 1951; Zumbo, Gadermann &amp; Zeisser, 2007). Unlike McDonald's ω, "
"GLB, or the Guttman λ family above (none of which require tau-equivalence), "
"α is biased -- usually downward -- whenever this assumption fails."
msgstr ""

