"ω total is the proportion of total-score variance explained by a fitted "
"factor model, computed from the model's actual loadings rather than assuming "
"they are equal (McDonald, 1999). ω hierarchical (ωₕ) is the narrower "
"quantity: the variance attributable specifically to ONE general factor "
"running through all items, net of whatever group-factor (subscale) variance "
